From: Illia Komsa <ik@fungamer.co>
Subject: [PATCH] LibGfx: cap a typeface's cached fonts at 32, evicting unused ones first

Gfx::Typeface kept up to 129 fonts, one per size, variation and feature
set, each with its HarfBuzz font and, on a variable font with an optical
size axis, a typeface clone. A font-size transition asks for a new size
every frame, so the cache stayed full of sizes nothing used, and the
eviction picked whichever entry came first in the hash table, in use or
not. karouka's pages use at most ~20 sizes of one typeface. Cap the cache
at 32 and evict a font only the cache holds before one still in use.

diff --git a/Libraries/LibGfx/Font/Typeface.cpp b/Libraries/LibGfx/Font/Typeface.cpp
index cf48a7290c..80d660af5b 100644
--- a/Libraries/LibGfx/Font/Typeface.cpp
+++ b/Libraries/LibGfx/Font/Typeface.cpp
@@ -98,9 +98,23 @@ NonnullRefPtr<Font> Typeface::font(float point_size, FontVariationSettings const
 
     // FIXME: It might be nice to have a global cap on the number of fonts we cache
     //        instead of doing it at the per-Typeface level like this.
-    constexpr size_t max_cached_font_size_count = 128;
-    if (m_fonts.size() > max_cached_font_size_count)
-        m_fonts.remove(m_fonts.begin());
+    // A font whose size changes by a fraction every frame (a font-size transition) asks for a new
+    // size each frame, and each size keeps its own HarfBuzz font and, on a variable font, a
+    // typeface clone for its optical size. The pages karouka renders use at most ~20 sizes of one
+    // typeface, so 32 bounds that churn without evicting a page's working set. Evict a font only
+    // this cache holds first: evicting one still in use frees nothing and would make a second
+    // copy of it on its next lookup.
+    constexpr size_t max_cached_font_count = 32;
+    if (m_fonts.size() >= max_cached_font_count) {
+        auto victim = m_fonts.begin();
+        for (auto it = m_fonts.begin(); it != m_fonts.end(); ++it) {
+            if (it->value->ref_count() == 1) {
+                victim = it;
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+        m_fonts.remove(victim);
+    }
 
     RefPtr<Typeface const> used_typeface = const_cast<Typeface*>(this);
     if (!variations.is_empty()) {
